        <Sticky classid="Sticky" id="2112554084" x="1188" y="72" w="468" h="216" colors="0, 15792890">
          <paramlist>
            <param name="full_font" value="Tahoma, 9pt" />
            <param name="align" value="0" />
            <param name="style" value="1" />
            <param name="font" value="1" />
            <param name="fg_color" value="0" />
            <param name="bg_color" value="15792890" />
            <param name="arrows" value="0" />
            <param name="opacity" value="25" />
            <param name="fg_color_adv" value="#FF000000" />
            <param name="bg_color_adv" value="#FFFAFAF0" />
            <param name="hl_color_adv" value="#FFFFFF00" />
            <param name="bdr_color_adv" value="#FF95918C" />
          </paramlist><![CDATA[Note: The cap limit bypass compensates for the d axis current required to neutralize the power flow from the filter capacitor in steady state. The rational behind this implementation is that a general current limit would apply to the rating of the device at the POI, and not strictly to the current loop control, which would necessarily yield less than the rating due to the capacitor in the LCL filter. 
This value is sampled when the current limiting is enabled and held constant, so as to not change during transients. It is worth considering whether it ought to change during a transient, since the reactive power from the capacitor is a function of the voltage. 
This functionality is easily bypassed, and not included in the ideal limiting
]]></Sticky>
